    "launch_failure_rate": 0.7273,
    "operator_error": "When patching join deadlines by hand we initially misidentified which launches had succeeded and gave a 60-second join deadline to rank 7, which was in fact running. No false-positive failure resulted: rank 7 was calling into the runtime regularly, so every call renewed its lease and the deadline never expired. That is the lease mechanism behaving exactly as intended -- evidence of activity overrides a pessimistic deadline.",
    "observed": {
      "glossary_allreduce": "closed with the survivors after 17 of 22 ranks were declared failed",
      "rank2": "declared failed after 580s of silence. Rank 2 was instructed to run `ampi hb --extend 1200` before its long translation step and did not. This is the central operational finding of the run: executors do not reliably volunteer liveness information, so a protocol that depends on them doing so will kill working agents."
    }
